# Copy to .env for local development. Never commit the real .env file (already gitignored).
# See DEPLOYMENT.md for the full environment-configuration model.

# --- Server ---
PORT=3000
NODE_ENV=development
WEB_BASE_URL="http://localhost:3001"

# Comma-separated browser origins allowed to make credentialed (cookie-bearing) requests — see
# src/common/cors-origins.ts. Not required: production falls back to the known fastque.com +
# Railway web origins when unset, development falls back to localhost. Native mobile clients are
# never subject to CORS and are unaffected either way. Example:
#   CORS_ALLOWED_ORIGINS="https://fastque.com,https://barbercueweb-production.up.railway.app"
CORS_ALLOWED_ORIGINS=""

# --- Database (Phase 1: required for Prisma) ---
# Local dev example (adjust to your local/managed Postgres instance):
DATABASE_URL="postgresql://postgres:postgres@localhost:5432/barbercue_dev?schema=public"

# --- Auth (Phase 2) ---
JWT_ACCESS_SECRET="change-me-dev-only"
# AES key for encrypting User.totpSecret at rest (admin 2FA). Any long random string; rotating
# it invalidates every already-provisioned TOTP secret, so treat it like any other prod secret.
TOTP_ENCRYPTION_KEY="change-me-dev-only"

# --- Admin seed (Phase 2 — apps/backend/prisma/seed.ts; admin accounts are seeded, not self-serve) ---
ADMIN_SEED_EMAIL="admin@barbercue.app"
ADMIN_SEED_PASSWORD="change-me-dev-only"

# --- OTP provider (Phase 2 — customer phone-OTP auth; production SMS via 2Factor.in as of the
# resend-OTP/SMS-delivery phase). Not required in development: when NODE_ENV != "production" the
# dev ConsoleOtpSender logs the code to the server console instead. When NODE_ENV == "production",
# TwoFactorOtpSender is used instead and this MUST be set to a real 2Factor.in API key, or every
# OTP request will fail with OTP_DELIVERY_FAILED (see auth.module.ts / two-factor-otp-sender.ts).
# Never a real value here — real secrets are configured directly in the hosting platform (Railway),
# never committed. ---
OTP_PROVIDER_API_KEY=""

# --- Google Sign-In (major-upgrade phase) — customer auth, additive to phone OTP, never a
# replacement for it. These are OAuth *client IDs*, not secrets (Google never issues a client
# *secret* for this token-verification flow) — same public-but-server-validated shape as the
# public client IDs in apps/web/.env.example and apps/mobile/.env.example, which MUST match these
# exactly (same Google Cloud OAuth clients on every side). Without these set,
# GoogleAuthService.verifyIdToken always throws GOOGLE_TOKEN_INVALID — POST auth/google fails
# safely, closed, never silently accepts an unverifiable token. See ARCHITECTURE.md for the exact
# manual Google Cloud Console setup steps. ---
GOOGLE_WEB_CLIENT_ID=""
GOOGLE_ANDROID_CLIENT_ID=""

# --- AI Style Advisor (major-upgrade phase) — real hairstyle-preview generation. DISABLED by
# default: gemini-2.5-flash-image has NO free tier (confirmed on ai.google.dev/gemini-api/docs
# /pricing AND empirically — a real key returned HTTP 429 on the very first call), so
# StyleAdvisorModule's factory does NOT auto-select GeminiAiImageProvider just because
# GEMINI_API_KEY is set — every request gets AI_PROVIDER_NOT_CONFIGURED from
# UnconfiguredAiImageProvider (503, no fake preview) until you deliberately re-enable billing.
# Research into free hairstyle/virtual-try-on APIs found none that were both genuinely free
# (recurring quota, not a one-time trial) AND had a documented photo-retention policy we could
# verify without personally creating a third-party account — see ARCHITECTURE.md §19.
#
# To intentionally reactivate Gemini once you turn on billing, set BOTH of these (either alone
# does nothing):
GEMINI_API_KEY=""
# AI_IMAGE_PROVIDER=gemini            # explicit opt-in switch — see style-advisor.module.ts
#
# Get a key from Google AI Studio (https://aistudio.google.com/apikey) — a separate credential
# from the OAuth GOOGLE_WEB_CLIENT_ID above, billed per-image (~$0.039/generated image, 3 previews
# per request). Backend-only: never expose this as a NEXT_PUBLIC_*/EXPO_PUBLIC_* variable or send
# it to any client. Never a real value here — real secrets are configured directly in the hosting
# platform (Railway), never committed. ---

# --- Email provider (Phase 2 — forgot-password/staff-invitation emails, via Resend's HTTP API).
# Not required in development: ConsoleEmailSender logs the link instead of emailing it. In
# production, BOTH must be set or EMAIL_SENDER stays fail-closed (UnavailableProductionEmailSender)
# exactly as before — never a silent downgrade to the console capture. EMAIL_FROM_ADDRESS must be
# at a domain verified in the Resend dashboard (Domains -> Verify), or Resend rejects the send. ---
RESEND_API_KEY=""
EMAIL_FROM_ADDRESS=""

# --- Payments (Phase 4 — Razorpay UPI integration, not wired yet) ---
PAYMENT_PROVIDER_KEY_ID=""
PAYMENT_PROVIDER_KEY_SECRET=""
PAYMENT_WEBHOOK_SECRET=""

# --- Photo storage ---
# Launch driver: a Railway persistent Volume. LOCAL_STORAGE_DIR is the volume's mount
# path (e.g. "/data/salon-photos" on Railway; a local directory in dev).
# LOCAL_STORAGE_PUBLIC_BASE_URL is this backend's own externally reachable origin
# (no path) — files are served back out at "<that origin>/uploads/...".
# Both must be set together, or uploads are refused with a clear error; linking an
# existing https photo URL keeps working either way.
LOCAL_STORAGE_DIR=""
LOCAL_STORAGE_PUBLIC_BASE_URL=""

# --- Object storage (R2/S3 — an alternative to the volume above, not used at launch) ---
# Salon photo uploads. S3-compatible (Cloudflare R2 for V1 — see DEPLOYMENT.md).
# ALL FIVE must be set or uploads are refused with a clear error; linking an existing
# https photo URL keeps working either way.
OBJECT_STORAGE_BUCKET=""
OBJECT_STORAGE_KEY=""
OBJECT_STORAGE_SECRET=""
# R2: https://<account-id>.r2.cloudflarestorage.com
OBJECT_STORAGE_ENDPOINT=""
# The PUBLIC read URL the browser loads photos from — the bucket's r2.dev subdomain or
# your custom domain. NOT the same host as the endpoint above, which is write-only/signed.
OBJECT_STORAGE_PUBLIC_BASE_URL=""

# --- Web ISR revalidation webhook (later phase) ---
REVALIDATE_SECRET="change-me-dev-only"
